WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.700
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.702
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:03.737
We hope you're
doing well tonight

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:04.537
and now, if you don't mind,

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.905
we are going to get to the news.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.941
President Biden criticized
the GOP yesterday and said,

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:12.144
"This ain't your father's
Republican Party."

00:00:12.144 --> 00:00:15.782
Yeah, this one definitely feels
more like your uncle's.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.283
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.386
President Biden also said
that next week's midterms are

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.455
the "most important election
of our lifetime,"

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:25.458
and that's saying something,
coming from a guy who, maybe,

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.626
voted for Lincoln?

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:28.795
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.430
President Biden warned yesterday

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.432
that Republican
Senator Rick Scott wants

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:35.268
to cut Social Security
and Medicare, and added,

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.002
"Hot damn, boy!"

00:00:37.002 --> 00:00:39.806
By the way, using the phrase
"Hot damn, boy,"

00:00:39.806 --> 00:00:42.307
instantly qualifies you
for Medicare.

00:00:42.307 --> 00:00:44.043
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:47.179
At a campaign stop in Wisconsin,
Republican Senator Ron Johnson

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:50.049
said that he is not sure
if he will accept the results

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:52.184
of next week's
midterm elections, and added,

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:55.088
"Do Democrats have something
up their sleeves?"

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.989
Have you met Democrats?

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:59.993
They famously have nothing
up their sleeve.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:00.794
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.161
The best they can manage is

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.930
a quarter behind the ear.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.298
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:07.400
According to a new poll,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.669
just 10% of voters
under the age of 40

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.437
strongly approve
of President Biden,

00:01:11.437 --> 00:01:13.139
but mostly because people
under 40

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.274
don't really feel
strongly anymore.

00:01:15.274 --> 00:01:17.143
[ Laughter ]
Dave, your house is on fire!

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.645
"Alright, man, I don't know."

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.979
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.947
Agriculture
Secretary Tom Vilsack

00:01:21.947 --> 00:01:24.250
told reporters yesterday
that the country is facing

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.218
a turkey shortage.
Oh, no!

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:27.987
You mean we might not get
to have

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.623
the world's driest meat
this Thanksgiving?

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.058
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:35.361
What's next, a shortage on the
raisins that ruin stuffing?

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:37.163
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:41.000
Under a new pay transparency law
that took effect yesterday,

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.236
New York City employers
are now required

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:45.872
to disclose salary ranges
in all job listings,

00:01:45.872 --> 00:01:48.074
which was a humiliating way

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.642
to find out Wally makes more
than me.

00:01:50.642 --> 00:01:53.947
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.814
A fire broke out early yesterday

00:01:55.814 --> 00:01:57.817
at New York City's
Museum of Natural History

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.385
and took about an hour
to contain.

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.954
It took so long because none
of the rescue personnel

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:04.356
could figure out where they were
on the free map.

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:08.328
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:11.497
Starbucks will begin offering
its holiday drink cups tomorrow.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:13.566
That story again --
tomorrow marks the start

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:14.734
of the war on Christmas.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.169
"Plain red?!

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:17.270
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.239
Do Jesus and Santa know
about this?!"

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.307
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.875
And, finally,
according to new reports,

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.744
staff morale at CNN is
at an all-time low

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:28.280
as the network undergoes
a cost-cutting overhaul.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.551
In related news, get ready
for the new season of...

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:36.589
[ Laughter ]
And that was the monologue,
everybody!

